how far it goes beyond the simple examples.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.840
So, to start off at least, rather than making&nbsp;
explicit calculations, let's just simulate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.620
things by running a large number of samples&nbsp;
and letting the total number of results in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.880
each different outcome give us some sense for&nbsp;
what that distribution looks like. As I said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

